| Small depot generator 20 -> 40 power/s | 150 | 30 | c07; large core already has 40 |

Faster processing has proportionally higher instantaneous power demand and unchanged per-unit chemistry/energy at these tiers. Transport hull upgrades must commission/replace the actual template and obey its existing costs and fuel math; a terminal upgrade does not magically improve a ship's Isp or tank mass. Higher tiers never restore condition, refill storage, replenish a deposit or duplicate a starter kit. Advanced generator, battery and solar output/capacity remain their explicit section values. Use baseline reference stats for every multiplier to avoid compounded accidental boosts.


Validation runs before gameplay: campaign prerequisite graph acyclic; every reward/objective references a defined ID; baseline kit reaches c01 without imported construction materials; c02 reachable near KSC and at distant supported sites through baseline bank expansion within deck limits; first Metal/bin/shop construction has no Parts dependency cycle; capacity can hold each next-tier material recipe; every required transport unlock precedes objectives that require it; rates/costs finite and nonnegative; LF/OX densities/mixture valid; endpoint orbit/role supports each transport; no free propellant in building/vehicle commissioning; time/payload positive; recipe duplicate rates aggregated; body profile fallbacks defined; localization keys present. Invalid optional definitions are disabled with a diagnostic; invalid baseline/campaign definitions block that subsystem rather than silently accepting impossible quests.

